WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.323 --> 00:00:16.544
wanted to refuse the ghost's invitation.

2
00:00:17.625 --> 00:00:20.926
He had no desire to walk anywhere with such a frightening creature!

3
00:00:21.887 --> 00:00:23.388
But it was pointless to resist.

4
00:00:24.989 --> 00:00:29.911
The ghost's grasp was as gentle as a child's hand, but it was stronger than the grip of

5
00:00:29.991 --> 00:00:30.572
any adult.

6
00:00:32.072 --> 00:00:34.674
The ghost pulled Scrooge toward one of the windows.

7
00:00:34.694 --> 00:00:37.155
"Wait, spirit!"

8
00:00:37.615 --> 00:00:38.376
Scrooge cried.

9
00:00:38.396 --> 00:00:41.777
"I'm a mortal, not a ghost, remember?

10
00:00:42.958 --> 00:00:44.319
And we're on the second floor.

11
00:00:45.419 --> 00:00:48.001
If I fall out the window, I'll get hurt!"

12
00:00:48.021 --> 00:00:52.163
"Don't worry," the ghost said.

13
00:00:53.604 --> 00:00:55.145
He touched Scrooge on his heart.

14
00:00:55.165 --> 00:01:01.088
"My touch on your heart is all it takes to keep you safe."

15
00:01:03.020 --> 00:01:06.641
With that, both spirit and Scrooge passed through the wall.

16
00:01:08.702 --> 00:01:13.923
Instead of emerging onto the street in front of the apartment building, they stood on an open road.

17
00:01:14.784 --> 00:01:16.484
The city and night had vanished.

18
00:01:17.605 --> 00:01:19.905
It was now a cold winter day in the country.

19
00:01:21.366 --> 00:01:26.347
Snowy fields lay on either side of the road, and the air felt clear and crisp.

20
00:01:26.367 --> 00:01:29.068
"Good heavens!"

21
00:01:29.544 --> 00:01:32.545
Scrooge cried, clasping his hands as he looked around.

22
00:01:32.565 --> 00:01:35.547
"I know exactly where we are.

23
00:01:36.947 --> 00:01:38.808
I grew up in this place!"

24
00:01:40.529 --> 00:01:43.610
The Ghost of Christmas Past touched Scrooge's heart again.

25
00:01:45.350 --> 00:01:49.112
Scrooge gasped as various pleasant odors floated past his nose.

26
00:01:50.673 --> 00:01:53.714
Each one reminded him of the few happy moments from his childhood.

27
00:01:56.115 --> 00:01:58.636
There was the scent of his mother's lavender perfume.

28
00:02:00.188 --> 00:02:04.090
Then came the buttery aroma of the cookies his nanny had baked for him.

29
00:02:05.650 --> 00:02:09.592
Next he smelled the sweetness of his beloved sister's favorite candy.

30
00:02:09.612 --> 00:02:15.914
"Your lip is trembling," the ghost said in its mild voice.

31
00:02:15.934 --> 00:02:20.696
"And what is that upon your cheek?"

32
00:02:20.716 --> 00:02:23.858
Scrooge touched his cheek, which felt moist with tears.

33
00:02:23.878 --> 00:02:27.479
"Never mind," he said with a catch in his voice.

34
00:02:27.499 --> 00:02:29.740
"Lead me where you wish."

35
00:02:32.268 --> 00:02:33.809
"Don't you remember the way?"

36
00:02:34.409 --> 00:02:35.389
the spirit asked.

37
00:02:35.409 --> 00:02:39.851
"I do remember," Scrooge said.

38
00:02:41.372 --> 00:02:44.113
His feet carried him quickly along the road to a town.

39
00:02:47.235 --> 00:02:52.537
Scrooge recognized the bridge over the river, the church steeple, and everything else he saw.

40
00:02:54.898 --> 00:02:59.480
They passed a pair of shaggy ponies trotting along with laughing boys on their backs.

41
00:03:00.988 --> 00:03:05.591
Scrooge recognized the boys as well, though by now, they should be old men like him.

42
00:03:07.673 --> 00:03:10.334
He called out to them, but they didn't respond.

43
00:03:13.997 --> 00:03:17.759
people are shadows of things that have been," the ghost said.

44
00:03:17.779 --> 00:03:20.261
"They can't see or hear us."

45
00:03:20.281 --> 00:03:26.665
"I see," Scrooge said, watching more happy people go by.

46
00:03:26.686 --> 00:03:29.387
"Merry Christmas!"

47
00:03:30.600 --> 00:03:33.521
An older man tipped his hat to several young ladies.

48
00:03:33.541 --> 00:03:36.882
"And a merry Christmas to you, sir!"

49
00:03:37.402 --> 00:03:38.962
the ladies said with good cheer.

50
00:03:41.643 --> 00:03:46.164
Finally Scrooge reached a house that was even more familiar than the rest.

51
00:03:47.565 --> 00:03:50.665
In front of it, a young boy was building a snowman.

52
00:03:53.626 --> 00:03:55.147
Scrooge's eyes widened.

53
00:03:55.167 --> 00:03:59.528
"Why, that that boy is me!"

54
00:04:01.460 --> 00:04:05.581
The young Ebenezer finished the snowman by placing a hat on its head.

55
00:04:06.641 --> 00:04:08.902
Then he grinned and ran into the house.

56
00:04:12.063 --> 00:04:16.384
A moment later he reappeared, pulling a laughing young woman by the hand.

57
00:04:17.624 --> 00:04:19.865
She was holding a baby wrapped in a blanket.

58
00:04:19.885 --> 00:04:23.586
"Oh," Scrooge whispered.

59
00:04:23.606 --> 00:04:27.487
"It's my mother—she's alive again.

60
00:04:28.787 --> 00:04:33.201
My beautiful, kind mother, and my dear little sister too."

61
00:04:35.561 --> 00:04:36.442
"Look, Mother!"

62
00:04:37.082 --> 00:04:39.082
Young Ebenezer was grinning proudly.

63
00:04:39.102 --> 00:04:42.723
"I built a snowman for baby Fan!"

64
00:04:42.743 --> 00:04:47.465
"It's wonderful, my clever son," Mother said.

65
00:04:48.685 --> 00:04:51.366
She held up the baby so tiny Fan could see too.

66
00:04:52.826 --> 00:04:55.447
The baby cooed and waved her plump arms.

67
00:04:57.728 --> 00:05:02.053
Suddenly a large man burst out of the house, scowling at the scene.

68
00:05:02.073 --> 00:05:04.994
"What's going on out here?

69
00:05:06.234 --> 00:05:08.895
It's far too cold to be outdoors without proper clothes!"

70
00:05:08.915 --> 00:05:12.376
"It's all right, darling," Mother said quickly.

71
00:05:12.396 --> 00:05:15.117
"I came out for only a moment.

72
00:05:15.657 --> 00:05:18.378
Ebenezer wanted to show his snowman to Fan and me.

73
00:05:18.498 --> 00:05:19.158
That's all."

74
00:05:19.178 --> 00:05:22.759
"Humbug!" the man snapped.

75
00:05:22.779 --> 00:05:25.520
"Ebenezer should be indoors, reading.

76
00:05:26.508 --> 00:05:31.852
What sort of businessman will he become while wasting time on silly activities like building snowmen?

77
00:05:32.832 --> 00:05:34.233
And is that my best hat?"

78
00:05:36.075 --> 00:05:38.076
His face turned red with outrage.

79
00:05:39.777 --> 00:05:44.941
Then he stomped over and grabbed the hat off the snowman, accidentally knocking off its head.

80
00:05:44.961 --> 00:05:47.642
"Get inside, all of you.

81
00:05:48.443 --> 00:05:50.925
If the baby gets sick, I'll blame you, boy!"

82
00:05:53.326 --> 00:05:55.628
Scrooge shuddered along with his younger self.

83
00:05:57.036 --> 00:06:02.738
"I remember that day," he said as he watched young Ebenezer slink back into the house behind his

84
00:06:02.778 --> 00:06:10.920
parents. "A short time later, my father sent me off to boarding school."

85
00:06:12.180 --> 00:06:13.361
The ghost nodded.

86
00:06:13.381 --> 00:06:15.541
"Come with me.

87
00:06:16.262 --> 00:06:17.742
We have much more to see."

88
00:06:19.563 --> 00:06:23.884
After one last glance at the sad, headless snowman, Scrooge obeyed.
